WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.800
- Wait, is this like the Venus flytrap?

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.633
Is that what that is?

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:04.129
What's that thing called, what are those?

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.130
- I think it's a Venus flytrap.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:05.963
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:06.840
I like that you're wearing it.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.673
- Thank you.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.180
- It's like great,
metaphorically speaking,

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.013
when you meet people. (Kelly chuckles)

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:10.846
It's beware.

00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:11.679
- Yeah, it's like "I'll eat you up."

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:12.540
- Yeah. (Kelly laughs)

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.038
Welcome back. I have to ask you.

00:00:14.038 --> 00:00:14.880
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.260
- Every time we have you
here I ask you about your

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.690
pole dancing 'cause you're
like getting really good at it.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.523
- I'm not.

00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:20.356
- [Kelly] You're not?

00:00:20.356 --> 00:00:21.300
- No.
- I saw your video,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.230
your latest video.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.150
- No. I'm pretty bad.
- Girl, that's really hard.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.620
- It's hard, but I'm also bad.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:26.857
- I have tried and I was like

00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:28.530
"some things aren't meant for me."

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.400
- Listen.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.710
Kelly, it is okay to be bad at stuff.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.543
- Oh, I'm amazingly
bad at a lot of things.

00:00:32.543 --> 00:00:37.498
- I'm just trying to normalize
being bad at things you like.

00:00:37.498 --> 00:00:38.331
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:38.331 --> 00:00:40.800
Like I have fun, but like
by no means am I sexy.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.633
I truly like...

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:42.960
- Well, I don't agree with that.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.793
- Oh, come on.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.240
I don't agree with that, Ms. White Boots.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.559
I saw that post...
(Nicole laughs)

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:47.879
- My little white hooker boots.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:50.703
- Yeah. I was like, "all right!"

00:00:50.703 --> 00:00:53.186
Like I could not physically do that.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.019
- Oh yeah, there-

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:57.244
(audiences cheers)
(Nicole laughs)

00:00:57.244 --> 00:00:58.564
- [Kelly] That's a workout.

00:00:58.564 --> 00:00:59.585
- [Nicole] It is a workout.

00:00:59.585 --> 00:01:01.290
- [Kelly] That is a workout.
- The boots, they're pretty

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:02.204
good.

00:01:02.204 --> 00:01:03.037
Look at her, catching herself on the...

00:01:03.037 --> 00:01:04.020
Like, I can't do that.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:05.490
- Well I also narrate,
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.230
I like to narrate my videos

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.850
just so everyone knows what's going on.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.897
It's just like, "Ooh,
she's breathing heavy."

00:01:10.897 --> 00:01:12.187
"Ooh, she's tired."

00:01:12.187 --> 00:01:15.780
"Uh-oh. Will she make it
up the pole? Probably not."

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.430
- How are the comedy shows going though?

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.300
- Pretty good.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.133
- Yeah.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.460
- I mean... the crowds are back.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.293
It's nice.

00:01:21.293 --> 00:01:22.680
- It's fun, the energy. Yeah.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.530
- I've been doing a lot of
improv and that's the nicest

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.660
because you don't have
to prepare anything.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:28.590
- I love improv.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:29.640
I love watching it.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.473
- Would you ever do it?

00:01:30.473 --> 00:01:32.190
- I don't know, but I
think I would do that

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.300
before anything else
- Do you want to?

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.730
Because I can get, I could hook you up.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:36.582
- I would maybe try it.

00:01:36.582 --> 00:01:37.436
(audience cheers)

00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:38.269
- Would you?!

00:01:38.269 --> 00:01:39.102
- I think it would be fun.

00:01:39.102 --> 00:01:40.350
(audience cheers and claps)

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.910
I like acting on stage.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.130
Like I grew up in musical
theater and like theater.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.820
And I like doing it the one
time and you're in the mode.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:48.653
Like that's...

00:01:48.653 --> 00:01:50.040
- This is one time,
- That energy I'm into.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.000
- and you never do it again.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.833
- I know. So, it's fun that way.

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:53.910
- And if it's bad, there's
someone else on stage

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:54.743
to be like,

00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:56.610
"Hey friend... let's do something else."

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.620
- But even if it's bad, it's funny.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.455
- I think so.

00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:01.500
- Okay. Kelly, I'm holding you to this.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.760
You're going to do an improv show with me.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.310
- I'm going to be like
nervous but I would do it.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.780
- Really?!
- Just for fun.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.980
Like, I've never done it.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.200
- Well, I mean, you're not
doing it for money. (laughs)

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.033
- No. I just-

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.570
- Nobody gets paid to do
improv. (Kelly laughs)

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.860
It's all imaginary.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.693
- I didn't mean for my-
- This is me

00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:15.837
paying you for improv.

00:02:15.837 --> 00:02:20.144
- No, I meant like I've never
done anything like that.

00:02:20.144 --> 00:02:20.977
- This is exciting.
- Like other than

00:02:20.977 --> 00:02:21.810
like in high school doing... Yeah.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:22.643
- I'm gonna hold you to this.

00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:24.270
- So, do you do this with friends?

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.320
- I do it with friends.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.520
Lately, Seth Rogan,

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.907
has joined the show that I do.
- He's hilarious.

00:02:28.907 --> 00:02:30.750
He was just on here.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.960
I'll tell you what I did
not realize about him.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.490
I knew he had a great laugh

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.770
but like it is the most

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:40.410
infectious and like you
end up laughing so much

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.240
at his laugh you can't stop.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.890
- Yeah, on stage, sometimes you'll like

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.020
get into a giggle fit 'cause
you'll hear his giggle

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.775
and you're like, "Ooh, I am being funny."

00:02:47.775 --> 00:02:48.608
(audience laughs)
- Oh my God.

00:02:48.608 --> 00:02:49.500
And his laugh,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.120
I've never heard anything like it.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:51.953
- It's great.

00:02:51.953 --> 00:02:53.130
- So, you do it with friends whenever

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:53.963
you're up there.

00:02:53.963 --> 00:02:55.440
So, that's kind of, that's comfortable.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.273
- [Nicole] Yeah, we do this show...

00:02:56.273 --> 00:02:57.106
- You kind of feed off of each other.

00:02:57.106 --> 00:02:58.230
- It's called The Last Improv Show.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.250
It's like twice a month.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.083
Honestly...

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:01.260
I'm gonna get you to do it.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.093
- Okay.

00:03:02.093 --> 00:03:02.970
- I think you're gonna have fun.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.860
- Okay. I say yes to
things now that I never...

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:05.809
Well like this show... (chuckles)

00:03:05.809 --> 00:03:07.037
(everyone laughs)

00:03:07.037 --> 00:03:08.190
that I never would've said yes to before.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.356
- Yeah, sure. I'll host a show.

00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:11.610
- Even if I fail, when you
get older, you don't care.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.440
So you, I actually don't know that I cared

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.572
in my 20s either.

00:03:14.572 --> 00:03:15.405
(Nicole laughs)

00:03:15.405 --> 00:03:17.430
But you have some interesting merchandise

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.340
with your comedy shows, but
this one's is pretty great.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.043
What do you thinks happening here, Nicole?

00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:23.212
- So... (Nicole laughs)

00:03:23.212 --> 00:03:24.591
- What do you thinks happening there?

00:03:24.591 --> 00:03:25.877
- There's a lot.

00:03:25.877 --> 00:03:28.271
And so little happening
between, like behind my eyes.

00:03:28.271 --> 00:03:31.110
- She's nervous and maybe angry.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:31.943
I don't know what's happening.

00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:32.880
- She's (bleep).

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.590
- Oh... yeah.
(Audience laughs)

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:39.030
- I was in... (laughs) I
was in upstate New York

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.000
with my friend Christi
and she asked someone

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.420
to take our picture and
that is what my face did.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.827
- I am so happy right
now and I am keeping this

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:49.660
(Nicole laughs)

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.630
and I will be wearing it when I do improv.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.181
- Please do.

00:03:53.181 --> 00:03:54.014
(audience claps and cheers)

00:03:54.014 --> 00:03:56.010
- This is my uniform. (laughs)

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.870
- Yeah, somebody asked, they were like,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.137
they found that picture
and they were like...

00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:02.160
"Can this be on merch?" and
I was like, "Yeah, why not?"

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.380
- Now, we can all have her face looking

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.810
whatever kind of feeling or
emotion you think she's in...

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.950
What state?
(Nicole chuckles)

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:08.783
You can just pick.

00:04:08.783 --> 00:04:11.160
- I was having a good time,
but it doesn't look like it.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.870
It looks like I was being kidnapped.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.904
- Yeah, that's what (laughs)

00:04:14.904 --> 00:04:15.930
it's like serious or anxious.
- Like I'm not okay.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.700
- Yeah... Well, speaking of old photos,

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.430
this is your Instagram
profile pic. (audience laughs)

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.420
So, wait, what's happening?

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.800
Was this the end of the night?

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.960
- That might have been
the middle of the night.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.460
I actually don't know.
- I love you.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.830
- I was with my two best
friends from high school

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.570
and I think I just started twerking

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.340
and then money started flying
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.390
and then I wiggled around

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.090
on the floor and then kept all the money.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:36.923
- Hell yeah.

00:04:36.923 --> 00:04:37.756
- [Nicole] I was working.

00:04:37.756 --> 00:04:39.550
- Yeah. They threw it,
you know, it's fair game.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.680
- Yeah. It's mine now.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.513
- Fair game.

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:43.890
So, what do you think
made you fall in love

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.630
with performing at first?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.030
- Well, it wasn't like me
who fell in love with it.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.137
My mom was like, "Why don't
you try out for the play?"

00:04:50.137 --> 00:04:51.337
"You talk a lot."

00:04:51.337 --> 00:04:53.490
"Why don't you just like
go talk on a stage?"

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.080
And I was like, "Okay."

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.330
Because I had undiagnosed ADHD,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.820
And people are mean to
you when you're chatty.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.900
So, I did this play and it was
like a bunch of short plays

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.340
by Christopher Durang

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.170
and the first time I made people laugh,

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.510
I was like (bleep) powerful.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.343
- Yeah.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:11.220
- I love this.
- It feels good, yeah.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.240
- It felt so good.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.717
So, then from that day on, I was like

00:05:13.717 --> 00:05:15.428
"I'm gonna be a thespian."

00:05:15.428 --> 00:05:16.440
- A thespian?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.210
- Yeah. But I also did track and field.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.419
I did the fat girl sport, shot put and-

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:23.010
- (Kelly laughs)

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.397
- 'Cause whenever I say I
did track, people are like,

00:05:24.397 --> 00:05:25.357
"No, you didn't" and I'm like,

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.480
"Yes, I did, I threw the thing."

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.313
- Shot put, yeah. (chuckles)

00:05:28.313 --> 00:05:30.060
- Yes, the big, you
wanna find the big girls

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:30.930
on a track field.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.230
We're in the little circle
over there with a big thing.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.350
- Also, the ones that you do
not wanna get in a fight with.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.878
- Oh, no, it'll (bleep) you
up if it hits you in the head.

00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:37.714
(Kelly laughs) My God.

00:05:37.714 --> 00:05:38.547
(Kelly and audience clapping)

00:05:38.547 --> 00:05:41.400
- Just like, (imitates explosion)

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.577
my track coach was like,

00:05:42.577 --> 00:05:44.857
"I mean if you just like
applied yourself..."

00:05:44.857 --> 00:05:46.260
"You could be like a state champion."

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.060
I was like, "Sorry, I'm on a stage."

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.040
- Do they clap for you there?

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:50.873
Yeah. You're like-

00:05:50.873 --> 00:05:52.680
- They don't clap for
you when you're throwing

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.030
the shot put...

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.670
It like lands with a thud
and everyone's like "Okay."

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.280
- The only time you get clapped
for at a track and field

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.350
is when you're like
the last one finishing.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.786
And they're like, "You can do it!"

00:06:02.786 --> 00:06:03.810
- "You can do it!" Yeah.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.130
- It's the only time you're getting the

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.480
green participation ribbon.
(Nicole laughs)

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.730
So, what's new this season
on your show "Grand Crew"?

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:12.180
- Okay, so the last
episode we went to Ojai

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.030
which is like a very fun vacation episode.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.890
And then, it's like a
"will they, won't they?"

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.570
With Fay and Anthony.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.330
And then my character, I
had a secret boyfriend.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.590
He is revealed.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.870
And then it's like, "do
they stay together?"

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.350
If you're watching, we don't. (both laugh)

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.240
And if you aren't watching...

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.540
- Spoiler alert!
- Spoiled it!

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.760
Get on with it, watch on Peacock.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.930
But let's see;

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.670
There's more stuff that
happens with like my career,

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.070
there's more stuff that
happens with my love life.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.810
It's just like a really fun season,

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.270
like we had a really
good time shooting it.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:45.210
- You have such a great cast.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.470
We've had so many people
on here from the show.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.389
- I love that.

00:06:47.389 --> 00:06:48.222
- It's so good, yeah.

00:06:48.222 --> 00:06:49.140
Great chemistry.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.960
Your character runs into some
pretty awkward situations.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.310
- Yes.
- With men.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:54.480
Have you had any recently

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.785
that are fun to tell
on daytime television?

00:06:56.785 --> 00:06:59.253
- Hmm, fun to tell on daytime?

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.620
I can think of several that you'd have to

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.510
bleep a lot of it, but...

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.156
- We're already gonna
have to bleep a couple...

00:07:05.156 --> 00:07:07.410
(both laugh)

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:08.243
- Like what do I do?

00:07:08.243 --> 00:07:10.080
- It's me too, you're good.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.937
- I went on a date with this
man who off the bat was like,

00:07:12.937 --> 00:07:13.980
"I don't know who you are."

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.530
Also, I was 20 minutes late. My bad...

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.600
And he was like so drunk.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.520
Like when I got there he was slurring

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.890
and like swaying and oversharing.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.433
- Can't hold his liquor 20 minutes? Okay.

00:07:24.433 --> 00:07:26.490
- I know, 20 minutes and all it took.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.852
But he was a short king and... (laughs)

00:07:28.852 --> 00:07:32.160
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:32.993
- [Nicole] Little guy.

00:07:32.993 --> 00:07:33.826
- I am one hundred percent

00:07:33.826 --> 00:07:36.060
stealing that, "A short king."

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:37.920
- He was very cute.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:41.123
But he kept insisting he didn't know me.

00:07:41.123 --> 00:07:41.956
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:07:41.956 --> 00:07:43.740
- And I was like, okay, that's odd.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:46.530
And then he was like, "Don't
talk about me on your podcast."

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.120
And I was like, "So you do know me?"

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.230
And he was like, "No!"

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.880
And I was like, "Then how do
you know I have a podcast?"

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:51.780
He's like, "My roommates!"

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.820
And I was like, "So your
roommates told you about like,

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.653
you know who I am."

00:07:54.653 --> 00:07:55.486
- [Kelly] So you know.

00:07:55.486 --> 00:07:56.730
- Yeah, and he was like,
"Just don't talk about me."

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.534
And I was like, "I absolutely will."

00:07:58.534 --> 00:07:59.940
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.190
I have to, you're being insane.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.120
- Great material.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.980
- And then he like offered
to drive me somewhere

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:06.540
and I was like, I don't think I should get

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.060
in the car with you and I
don't think you should drive.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.710
He was out of his mind.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.120
- Yeah, you know what though?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.800
Thank you for the sign right off the bat.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.120
Don't waste another day on that.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:15.953
- Yeah.

00:08:15.953 --> 00:08:18.630
But I did text him back when
he texted me the next day

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.823
because red flags to me (laughs)

00:08:21.823 --> 00:08:24.150
(audience laughing)

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.340
It's called desperation, you know?

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.173
- Oh my God.

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:28.775
I literally call myself
the red flag collector.

00:08:28.775 --> 00:08:31.050
(everyone laughs)

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.063
- It's a whole song about it.

00:08:32.063 --> 00:08:32.953
Anyway your-

00:08:32.953 --> 00:08:34.593
(Nicole and audience laugh)

00:08:34.593 --> 00:08:36.630
your show is kind of a throwback

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.670
to some of the nostalgic like 90s sitcoms.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.320
Which I love and I grew up on.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.430
So you're a big fan of those?

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.516
- Yeah, I love "Living Single," that is

00:08:43.516 --> 00:08:45.235
one of my favorite shows.

00:08:45.235 --> 00:08:46.068
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:08:46.068 --> 00:08:46.920
I love "Living Single."
- Yeah, right?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.363
It's just so good.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.250
I also love "Martin,"

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.510
I love "Sister Sister,"

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:52.343
like yeah.

00:08:52.343 --> 00:08:53.663
I just love 90s sitcoms and-

00:08:53.663 --> 00:08:54.960
- They're so good.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:55.793
- Yeah.

00:08:55.793 --> 00:08:56.626
And this like feels like an homage.

00:08:56.626 --> 00:08:57.870
Like we have a theme song.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.703
- Yeah.

00:08:58.703 --> 00:08:59.561
- A lot of shows don't have theme songs,

00:08:59.561 --> 00:09:00.618
it like gets into it.
- I know,

00:09:00.618 --> 00:09:01.650
and there were so many
great ones back then.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:02.483
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:09:02.483 --> 00:09:03.316
And this one's fun.

00:09:03.316 --> 00:09:05.760
It's done by our creator,
Phil Augusta Jackson

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.020
who also does music and stuff.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:07.853
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:09:07.853 --> 00:09:08.686
- So yeah,

00:09:08.686 --> 00:09:09.720
I love that it's like a throwback.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.190
- Well the representation on "Grand Crew"

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:13.170
extends itself behind the camera, right?

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.003
- Mm-hmm.

00:09:14.003 --> 00:09:14.836
- That was important?

00:09:14.836 --> 00:09:17.010
- Yeah, we have a lot of people
of color behind the scenes,

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.910
the writer's room is filled

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.560
with like black and brown people.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.620
But I like don't wanna
highlight that part of it,

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.180
because it is just like a sitcom.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.860
Like nobody called
"Friends" a white sitcom.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.720
Do you know what I mean?

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:27.553
(Kelly laughing)

00:09:27.553 --> 00:09:28.386
Like that would be insane.

00:09:28.386 --> 00:09:31.170
- Yeah, I just mean overall
shows are being more

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.003
like inclusive in general.

00:09:32.003 --> 00:09:32.836
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:09:32.836 --> 00:09:34.350
- Which I do think is really great.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.240
- But I just wanna tell
everybody that it is

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.610
an accessible show and
if you're white, you-

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:39.443
- [Kelly] You'll laugh too.

00:09:39.443 --> 00:09:41.940
- You'll laugh and if you
don't like black people

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.261
maybe you will after 30 minutes.

00:09:43.261 --> 00:09:46.094
(everyone laughs)

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.173
You're just like "they're not so bad."

00:09:48.173 --> 00:09:51.217
- That's the greatest slogan like tease,

00:09:51.217 --> 00:09:52.423
"maybe you'll like..."

